<HR COLOR="Orange">

<div align="center">


<p></p>
<table align="center" width="90%">
<tr><th colspan="2"><strong>Reassign Program</strong></th></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" colspan="2" align="center"><img src="images/reassign.gif"></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2">Periodically you may wish to change the ownership of a program from one position to another. For example, your New Jersey accounts may move from being controlled by New York to being controlled by your Atlantic Sea Board broker. This tool allows you to change the ownership of a particular program.
<p></p>
There are four steps you need to take to reassign a program.
</td></tr>

<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/1.gif"></td><td>The first thing you need to do is to select the position FROM which you wish to reassign the program. See below for details on the position search.  You can select only one.</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/2.gif"></td><td>Once you have selected the position from which you want to move the program, you need to search for and select the program or programs you want to move. The program search is identical to all other program searches, except it only shows programs that are currently owned by the position you selected in step one.</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/3.gif"></td><td>You then need to select the position to which you wish to transfer ownership of the program/s selected in step 2. The position search is the same as in step one.</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/4.gif"></td><td>When you click on "Reassign" the ownership of the program is transferred. The users in the first position will no longer be able to see the program, and the users in the final position will suddenly be able to see it.</td></tr>

</table>

<hr width="80%">

<table align="center" width="90%">
<tr><th colspan="2"><strong>Position Search</strong></th></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" colspan="2" align="center"><img src="images/user_position_search.gif"></td></tr>

<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/1.gif"></td><td>
You can enter several criteria to search for a user position. 
<ul>
<li><em>Zones:</em> Select from a list of zones</li>
<li><em>Region:</em> You can pick which region to search in</li>
<li><em>Market:</em> You may also select which market to look in</li>
<li><em>Positions Under:</em> If you make a selection from this list, you will see all the positions under the position you have selected.</li>
<li><em>Label:</em> Entering text will return all positions with a label similar to what you entered.
Click on [search position] when you are satisfied with your search criteria. Like all other searches, the more criteria you enter, the fewer results will be returned.</li>
</ul>
</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top"><img src="images/2.gif"></td><td>You should select a single position either to have programs transferred from it or to it. When you have made your selection, click on [import selected position] and the window will close.</td></tr>

</table>

<p></p>
</div>



